{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443893-the-inconnu-thread","id":1443893,"title":"The Inconnu thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-14T10:10:17-07:00","id":1443893,"title":"The Inconnu thread","content":"I just watched the Gentleman's Guide to the Inconnu and it was very interesting:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/CsnXIX05Tfk?list=FLfWmu27KD5LKzzySKDJidoA\" data-code=\"CsnXIX05Tfk\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/CsnXIX05Tfk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I've always struggled to use the Inconnu in games because I've never felt they were terribly interesting. The group was always too mysterious and removed for its own good so I didn't know how I could use it. Even the Castle Hunendora adventures felt a little weak for me. I think I got more use out of the True Black Hand, as silly as it may be, than I ever did the Inconnu. However, I feel like this version actually goes a long way into making them relevant to games.<br /> <br /> How do you see the Inconnu?<br /> <br /> How have you used them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T10:21:19-07:00","id":1443894,"title":"","content":"I read <i>Lair of the hidden</i> a few months ago, a good book with some interesting plots and complex characters, but hard to implement on most of ongoing chronicles and very based in the globetrotter Jyhad of the 90s. Anyway, the idea of a sect inside other sect as it is the Inconnu is interesting and less phantastic than the crossover-rainbow Tal-Mahe-Ra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 04-14-2021, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T11:14:09-07:00","id":1443900,"title":"","content":"I feel like The Inconnu are a sect that works best when they\u2019re styled to the flavor of conspiracy or secret society that suits the interest of the ST. I will include some of the ideas and options that occur to me.<br /> <br /> When I think about the Backstory of the Inconnu, I usually place their origins in the society of Rome. The vampiric senate of Rome would collapse alongside the empire as barbarians raid from the land and the split within the empire. As the vampiric society of europe collapsed into new fiefs, the neonates of the time learning to survive while many ancillae fled eastward to Byzantium and Persia. However the elders had their own intentions and would set out to achieve them from the shadows of europa.<br /> <br /> As time went on the society took on its new form as the Inconnu with a number of possible options:<br /> <br /> \u2022Power: the Inconnu strive to retain their power. The elders of the imperial senate have lurked in the shadow for over millenia. They have played the games of jyhad (the struggle) for centuries. They used the princes, dark kingdoms, and sects as pawns in their great game. The war of Camarilla against Sabbat, of Black Fiefs against Courts of Love; the Inconnu played the game of power.<br /> <br /> \u2022Enlightenment: the elders realized with the collapse of their power that nothing they could build could endure the crush of time and the press of humanity. They realized that they needed to pursue something higher. With news arriving from the east of the Salubri\u2019s pursuit of Golconda, they turn themselves to the study of it (whatever that is in your WoD). They monitor kindred society, trying to find those with the insight necessary to both teach them and others.<br /> <br /> \u2022Reconstruction: the elders of the senate were unable to endure the rapid changes of the empire\u2019s decline. Even after its fall they were too calcified to change. Akin to power, they have been lurking and are trying to recreate the vampiric society of Rome again. Perhaps for this reason they have helped to create and control the Camarilla as a recreation of Roman society.<br /> <br /> \u2022Salvation: as with enlightenment but instead of Golconda its other forms of religion. Probably Christianity; whether they define themselves in opposition to it or in pursuit of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T11:33:43-07:00","id":1443902,"title":"","content":"I had the same issue with the Inconnu that you did - how do you use them since they aren't doing anything? Their city Monitors were like the Watchers in Marvel Universe, they are there to witness and report, but don't have plans of their own. So I've never used them in game. I think they work well as a background element, but hard to effectively utilize. The easiest solution, of course, is to subvert it by having the Monitor violate their non-interference, but that just gets old and cancels out their definition.<br /> <br /> However, if I was ever going to do so, then I'd use them as the source to go to when you have some esoteric mystery that needs to be solved. The Inconnu probably has the answer the PC needs. And it's up to the PCs to track down someone from this mysterious organization and see if they can obtain the information from them. Less likely as part of a story I had planned, but more as a result of PCs developing a personal interest in something.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'd then need to come up with a way that the PCs could track one down, and at the moment I can't think of an interesting way to do that in game while retaining a sense of mystery.<br /> <br /> If I could think of movies or books that had similar plot to this, I might be able to mirror something as a gameable scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T12:04:24-07:00","id":1443909,"title":"","content":"The <i>Lair of the hidden</i> version of the Inconnu, based of the path of Golconda, could be useful in a chronicle about redemption, with the characters trying to regain their lost humanity, may the characters find some ancient grimoire of lost wisdom or some mysterious guide. The <i>Constantinople by night</i> version of the Inconnu, heirs of Rome and the eternal senate, could be more useful in political chronicles, with the conspiracies inside conspiracies trope. There is no only one Inconnu. Curiously, <i>Lair of the hidden, </i>was the only appearance of Saulot aside from the Transilvanian Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T12:05:43-07:00","id":1443910,"title":"","content":"If somebody took the golconda related loresheet, I could see bringing in the Inconnu as a sort of Mcguffin hunt. Find the Inconnu to help guide your next steps sorta thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T12:06:40-07:00","id":1443911,"title":"","content":"I like that the Master of Ravens/Malkavian Inconnu guy has become such an important part of V5. He's just spreading his completely wrong version of Golconda left and right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T12:18:06-07:00","id":1443914,"title":"","content":"Regarding the best use for the Inconnu in a chronicle, I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> is probably correct that &quot;source of obscure information&quot; is the most likely answer.<br /> <br /> To expand on that a bit, recently I started thinking of the Inconnu as kind of being like a Sect equivalent to Clan Nosferatu for isolationist Elders/Methuselahs. That is to say, it is primarily an information network. The Inconnu don't have an agenda as a Sect beyond enabling its members to pursue their own agendas through shared information. Which is why the &quot;leaders&quot; of the Inconnu, the Council of Twelve, has running the Monitor Network as the start and end of its listed authority. Other than that, it's just a place where various small ideologies and philosophies practiced by small numbers of Elders can group together for mutual support, kind of like the Disparate Alliance for Elder Vampires.<br /> <br /> Which is where my other answer for how to make interesting use of the Inconnu is to move on to the next step: what kind of Inconnu? Using the factions on the wiki as an example, a story with an Inconnu Seeker hiding in the city could be radically different from one with an Immaculate running rampant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T12:34:46-07:00","id":1443916,"title":"","content":"It always seemed to me that inconnu were, like, mostly pointless but maybe good if you wanted a mentor or something because they no doubt have weird tricks and it'd be a bit too weird if they really didn't want to sire anyone ever. The issue is that Pre-V5 the Camarilla were against religion so I could have fun with whatever secretive cult I wanted and not need to involve the inconnu (I suppose that's still true in V5, I just need to be a bit more extreme with it) <br /> To me the Inconnu along with the TBH just served to show you that there's a masquerade beyond your masquerade. They don't actually do anything except maybe occasionally compete for an artifact or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T13:02:44-07:00","id":1443921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443893-the-inconnu-thread?p=1443909#post1443909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>Lair of the hidden</i> version of the Inconnu, based of the path of Golconda, could be useful in a chronicle about redemption, with the characters trying to regain their lost humanity, may the characters find some ancient grimoire of lost wisdom or some mysterious guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Information about Golconda is the obvious reason to want to contact the Inconnu, but I think there needs to be other things like. Their isolation probably has a lot to do with avoiding the Jyhad, so things like information about lost Methusaleh (including some of their locations), lore about the antedeluvians, activities of non-vampires in the Jyhad like Horus, the secret masters of Ventrue belief, knowledge of the antedeluvian world, information about other obscure vampire sects (like the Children of Osiris, the True Black Hand, the Gehenna cults, or Baali), etc. would also be things the Inconnu should know and be reasons to want to contact them.<br /> <br /> I found the Dark Ages version of the Inconnu to simply be about Rome to be utterly bizarre and at odds with how they were presented in the original books. I never understood why they went that route. I could conceivably reconcile the two versions in my head, but I'm sure it would just be head canon as opposed to reflecting the purpose of the writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T13:23:32-07:00","id":1443924,"title":"","content":"The Dark Ages version is about ancient conspiracies as well, Rome fell, but the Senate Eternal not. Those ancient vampires, with long standing alliances (and feuds) did not just disappear, and in the XII century they are the Camarilla pre-Camarilla, the Inner Circle of the Long Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T13:27:38-07:00","id":1443925,"title":"","content":"I just figured they worked for/were pawns of the third generation. They keep track of things and take care of whatever needs tending while the ancients sleep, sort of like Marius. I realize the third gens are 13 or so Vampires with different aims, but a sect that keeps up with discoveries and goings on would be really useful to an antediluvian when he comes out of torpor. Do we really think they are all asleep all the time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T04:48:16-07:00","id":1444017,"title":"","content":"I have never used the Inconnu, and I'm unlikely to ever use them (or the True Black Hand). If I need a double extra secret vampire conspiracy for a plot, I just make my own.<br /> <br /> What I've come to understand from running VtM and Pathfinder adventures is that background material that players can never learn doesn't need to exist. If the Illuminati always kill on sight and never crack under interrogation, then the True Secret History of the Illuminati doesn't matter. Save your breath and write something people can play with. The purpose of a good conspiracy is to be unwound by the PCs, who then might agree and join, or disagree and fight. A conspiracy too shadowy to be found functionally doesn't exist. And Inconnu (and TBH) repeatedly sin by being better than you so that you never learn they existed in the first place.<br /> <br /> Size is also an issue. World-spanning conspiracies that have everyone wrapped around their fingers are just too much. Go smaller, like state-sized or clan-sized (a la Amici Noctis) conspiracies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T00:25:42-07:00","id":1444138,"title":"","content":"I also struggled a lot with these guys, but with the Gentelman's video and this forum and the years I've got a few headcanons:<br /> <br /> +The Inconnu want to: Control the Beast and Control the Blood. Mostly remove the negative parts of it, no matter how monstrous or incomplete this would make them.<br /> +Inconnu are looking for any way to circumvent or surpass the bad parts of being Elders and vampires (like, having high Blood Potency, lots of feeding limitations, high bane severity...), and Golconda is just the most talked about way. They study young vampires that might have interesting conditions or new wisdom that might subvert the curse, and watch the elders to see if any of them ever developed a way to cancel the banes and etc.<br /> +Thinbloods and Caitiffs are highly interesting, especially the mofing daywalking Thinbloods (although in my game I consider that they can walk only one hour before dusk, and one hour after dawn, but more than that is sun damage as default), for they are vampires (kinda) but don't suffer the banes of vampiredom. Caitiffs are like a bug in the system that cancel some things but if it could be controlled and weaponized, it could remove only the bad things (like Clan banes). <br /> +The Inconnu registers and studies all forms of Paths of Enlightenment, philosophies, humane or inhumane (wights too) vampire Convictions, looking for something that really digs deep in the soul, like supposedly Golconda does. And in this case I would think either Saulot hasn't reached it, haven't contacted the Inconnu, or has fallen out of it. And if the Wan Kuei hate Saulot, they despise the Inconnu and their roguish ass-stealing curiosity.<br /> +The Beckoning is driving the Inconnu nuts, because its like they have to find the way to control their blood pronto! Or else they will be dragged too to the conflict. Although some of them are already going to the Gehenna Crusade to see if they find any interesting struggles, eurekas, self-controlled elders...etc.<br /> +They don't get involved only in matters on getting into one side or another, but they aren't above releasing a Blood Plague and see those who survive to study their tenacity and blood. But they also are pro-Masquerade, and will either get the hell out of one city and call Inquisition on vampires who are causing too much ruckus to end it before it gets too much attention (they noticed the Inquisition, at least this one, also prefers to keep things quiet), or will give messages to those who should know about such breaches. Again, they might put a neonate in a Masquerade breaching situation (that the monitor has some control over) to see how it goes.<br /> +They think a vampire utopia is crazy talk, and will never work (we had 3 cities like that or more, and it simply never gets okay), and the Inconnu doesn't sounds like the collective living type, their quest seems something inner and not outer. They want to change their Blood and their Beast, not their surroundings.<br /> +&quot;A Beast I won't be, and the Beast I refute&quot; would be a rough slogan, they want total control of themselves. Frenzy and Hunger are like the thing they curse and spit upon every night.<br /> +They might be batshiet insane by now and have forgotten why they are collecting all this information, basically stuck on the automatic. I can see Elders and Methuselahs who aren't in the tightly knit intrigue, politics and survival games getting way too mental with their searches in the course of many millennia.<br /> +IF they could, they would probably do what Cappadocius tried to do, and devour God, for they would be capable of ending their own curses. But most don't want to have such high hopes taht such thing is possible so they prefer to rationalize that all that was lunatic talking of an ancient vampire (besides, it didn't work).<br /> +They are mostly jealous, jaded, old, tired, pissed and depressed about all this time and having so little progress in their search for freedom from the Beast. I suppose they get together in part to get each others hopes up with the slightest new possibility, otherwise they would fall to depression and defeatism, and end up falling to the Beast or letting the sun kiss them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T17:03:45-07:00","id":1444961,"title":"","content":"In hindsight, I view Lair of the Hidden as a satisfying punchline to a joke that took years to tell. It's just a dozen randos trapped in a castle, but they were so quiet that vampires spent centuries convincing themselves that they must be up to something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T20:22:20-07:00","id":1444982,"title":"","content":"I've never used them or been a player in a game where they were used. Squabbles between local elders, being hunted by mortal hunters, werewolf packs, invasions by the Camarilla/Sabbat/Anarchs, infernalist schemes, there are plenty of more exciting options than the Inconnu, and games generally end before STs have exhausted those options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T20:45:40-07:00","id":1444984,"title":"","content":"I've had Dracula show up multiple times as an Inconnu member and sometimes Rebekah.<br /> <br /> They are the only ones in 20 years of gaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T22:41:59-07:00","id":1444996,"title":"","content":"The Inconnu are a good plot seed to maybe have a mid-to-high tier coterie go on an objective to Diablerize them. It'd be extremely hard as hell, but a fun chronicle altogether to have it centered around. It'd also be interesting to have dynamic where the Inconnu attempt to go on a very uncharacteristic offensive-retaliatory motion against the coterie thereafter; even with the risk of maybe getting into war with any of the main Sects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T00:20:17-07:00","id":1445005,"title":"","content":"The Inconnu always felt like a relic from early VtM. Like, the idea was that Golconda and seeking to rid yourself of your vampiric nature and become human again, was going to be a common storyline for player characters, and so the Inconnu would be a way to work that into the campaign and you had the Inconnu scattered all over the place in cities so it would be easy for player characters to seek them out. But then basically nothing was ever done with them. I can't even remember if they got much mention at all between the first A World of Darkness book and Lair of the Hidden. They just ended up being an unexplained mystery box for so long that they ended up feeling fairly irrelevant, and then when we got the reveal in Lair of the Hidden they felt pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T00:32:51-07:00","id":1445009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443893-the-inconnu-thread?p=1445005#post1445005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inconnu always felt like a relic from early VtM. Like, the idea was that Golconda and seeking to rid yourself of your vampiric nature and become human again, was going to be a common storyline for player characters, and so the Inconnu would be a way to work that into the campaign and you had the Inconnu scattered all over the place in cities so it would be easy for player characters to seek them out. But then basically nothing was ever done with them. I can't even remember if they got much mention at all between the first A World of Darkness book and Lair of the Hidden. They just ended up being an unexplained mystery box for so long that they ended up feeling fairly irrelevant, and then when we got the reveal in Lair of the Hidden they felt pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>We got a couple of Monitors and the Ancient Rome origin for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T05:57:51-07:00","id":1445031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443893-the-inconnu-thread?p=1445005#post1445005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inconnu always felt like a relic from early VtM. Like, the idea was that Golconda and seeking to rid yourself of your vampiric nature and become human again, was going to be a common storyline for player characters, and so the Inconnu would be a way to work that into the campaign and you had the Inconnu scattered all over the place in cities so it would be easy for player characters to seek them out. But then basically nothing was ever done with them. I can't even remember if they got much mention at all between the first A World of Darkness book and Lair of the Hidden. They just ended up being an unexplained mystery box for so long that they ended up feeling fairly irrelevant, and then when we got the reveal in Lair of the Hidden they felt pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> The Inconnu gelled at lot more with early VtM, when <i>everything</i> was mysterious and undefined, and the journey to break the bonds of vampirism was a more central fixture of the game.<br /> <br /> But then the game started being more about 1) complex political machinations, 2) globe-trotting action, 3) ancient conspiracies, and 4) the forthcoming apocalypse. Many of the plot threads built around the maintenance of Humanity were left by the wayside (ex: the Children of Osiris, at least its vampiric side, being destroyed, and left only as a stub reference in the mortal Sorcerer books), and more attention was put on Paths of Enlightenment as the &quot;answer&quot; to the &quot;problem&quot; of Humanity.<br /> <br /> VtM never fully abandoned the search for Golconda, of course. But it became almost an afterthought. A token gesture the game maintained out of obligation, because it was a foundational element of the series.<br /> <br /> White Wolf tried to make the Inconnu relevant, but only later, when it seemed like the matter needed to be addressed before it was too late. Lair of the Hidden was an attempt to &quot;wrap up&quot; that dangling thread as the series geared up to its conclusion. Unfortunately, they hadn't really done anything up until that point to establish the Inconnu as an active force, much less hash out what their goals, methods, and capabilities were. They remained a hidden, unknown element, in a setting where everything was being defined and made actionable.<br /> <br /> So when Lair of the Hidden happened, people could be forgiven for thinking that the vampires of Hunedoara WERE the Inconnu, full stop. Rather than just one conspiracy within the larger web. It's not like fans were given anything else to go on. And while the work itself was extremely interesting and unlike anything else to be found in a VtM book, it didn't feel like it lived up to the hype that a decade+ of mystery had built up. It left players/Storytellers of the time thinking, &quot;wait, that's it?&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't know if anything could live up to that much hype, admittedly. But that's what you get for giving us nothing to go on during the interim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T06:18:56-07:00","id":1445036,"title":"","content":"As for how to handle the Inconnu in practice, I like how V20: Rites of the Blood does it. Presenting the Inconnu as less a sect or conspiracy, and more a scholarly and philosophical society of loosely aligned vampires. Ones who have realized that the Jyhad is bullshit, and that trying to play by its rules is a sucker's game. Rather, they try to stand outside the Jyhad, and work to achieve what TCG players like to call an &quot;Alternative Win Condition&quot;. In this case, mostly it means Golconda, though what that entails is disputed even within its ranks.<br /> <br /> It also means knowing as much as they can about the Jyhad. You can't transcend the cage if you do not know where its edges are. Hence, why their Monitors hang around, gathering information passively. The more they know the ins and outs of the Jyhad, the easier it is to avoid it. That gathering information also allows them to find useful recruits, and/or obtain lore/clues pertinent to their own personal studies, is a fringe benefit.<br /> <br /> So that presents a few ways they can be involved in a game. For one, Inconnu Monitors make it their business to know everything that goes on in their territory. If a PC wants to know something, the Monitor might know, meaning it's a good idea to get one on your side. Or, failing that, provide them with something they want, usually information, artifacts, or resources needed to remain apart from the wider Jyhad.<br /> <br /> For another, you might use them for their original purpose, and have them drop clues as to how to follow the path of Golconda. Or at least give aid to a PC struggling with their Humanity. An objective observer that can provide an unbiased perspective or substantive criticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T09:02:14-07:00","id":1445054,"title":"","content":"I would see the Inconnu pulled in two directions. <br /> <br /> First, as the &quot;competitors&quot; of the Camarilla's inner circle; Methuselah and the upper stratta of elders who want to guide the world of vampires on a certain course, one which isn't different enough to bother with open warfare, but perhaps enough that an occasional skirmish might abound. Perhaps they're the Illuminati to the Camarilla's Majestic 12 (Though, honestly, in terms of worldview it's probably the otherwayround) They act conservatively, seeming to do nothing, but on rare occasion they'll become a force of nature in their political interventions. Perhaps many of the great twists and turns throughout the eras have been at the direct instigation of the Inconnu, and another great upheval will occur soon, or perhaps their hand is more hidden, creating subtle changes and lending support for seemingly inconsequential squabbles. Or maybe they're more 'normal' and really just put supportive princes on the throne on occasion. <br /> <br /> Second, as a &quot;cult concerning enlightenment&quot;. Monitors primarily exist to search for genuine, worthy canidates to join their club. They're somewhat opposed to the Inner circle who promote secular beliefs to encourage stability, which is why they are very secretive. The Inconnu try to find peace with the kindred condition, to give them more direct philosophical opposition, I'd <b>bring back the Children of Osiris, </b>who famously seek to deny the beast and regain their humanity. <br /> <br /> Lesser (but still kinda good, and not at all exclusive) ideas include<br /> -Just making them a bunch of history nerds who seek to record EVERYTHING. <br /> -they're all actually mind-controlled by a single mythic figure.<br /> -they're a mythical scapegoat for anything wrong in the Camarilla. <br /> - Inconnu still don't perceive what they're doing as taking part in the Jyhad, because they're not engaged in personal struggle, they're in a sect-level struggle. <br /> -They abduct/ kill elders when they're getting to the point where they're strong enough to shake the world or challenge methuselah. <br /> -they're actually an anti-enlightenment cult, because enlightenment is dangerous. <br /> -It's mostly an elite social club that got way more attention than deserved, due to kindred being paranoid and unable to accept the idea that kindred would get together and not plot against others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:06:29-07:00","id":1445088,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Inconnu were from a time when the game developers presumed most players would want to play Louis and Nick Knight. Boy did they ever not read the room. Most people want to play Lestat or Dracula or Erik Northman or any number of vampires who reveled in their power and immortality. By and large, they wanted the same things they wanted in most games: to get rich and powerful by using their fantasy superpowers. Even those who eschewed violence often wanted to, say, become great poets or musicians while peacefully enjoying immortality with their eternal loves. The guys who wanted a cure to their superpowers and immortality were never a majority of the players.<br /> <br /> So the Inconnu became like those NPCs in World of Warcraft who everyone knows have poor quest rewards for hard quests: they just stand there ignored with yellow exclamation points over their heads. In fact I can kinda picture them if they were NPCs in an MMO.<br /> <br /> *Player clicks on Inconnu* &quot;Greetings adventurer, I have heard of your struggle to regain humanity, and I believe I can help, but first you will need to complete a series of quests...&quot;<br /> *Player starts to zone out, skips to the end of the speech, and reads the last line: &quot;Step one of the Achieve Golconda questline&quot;<br /> *Player minimizes the gamescreen and checks online for how the Achieve Golconda questline ends* &quot;that's a hardass questline, and it ends with...me becoming human?? Oh, screw this!&quot;<br /> *Player clicks Abandon Quest*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:11:17-07:00","id":1445090,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea that Monitors search for genuine, worthy candidates to join the Inconnu or perhaps to be introduced to the concepts of Golconda. I don't think that's the only or main reason - keeping up to date on the Jyhad and reporting their findings to other Inconnu is probably a more important task <i>in the setting</i>. But looking for candidates worthy of the secrets/lore of the Inconnu is probably their most important task <i>for an ST/gaming perspective</i>. It provides the excuse for an interaction with the PCs.<br /> <br /> That is an automatic hook. If one (or more) of the PCs appear serious about their Humanity, about Golconda, or about trying to transcend the Jyhad, then at some point an ST can decide to have the local Monitor contact her. (Alternately exchange that for whatever esoteric lore the PC is interested in - a Ventrue attempting to learn more about the Secret Masters; someone sympathetically researching the true history of the Salubri; looking for lore to help combat the Baali; or whatever).<br /> <br /> At that point, it's really a matter of how to make that an interesting experience. And to be able to do it in varied enough ways so that it doesn't seem like the same plot every time it happens. Does the Monitor use proxies, disguises, alternate identities, open, or concealing; is their approach direct, cryptic, helpful, manipulative; do they test the candidate, mentor them, just point the way, actively put challenges before them; do they just appear once, multiple times throughout the ages, or only when the candidates passes various stages; etc. An ST should have lots of different ways to differentiate such an approach even if they run this scenario 20 or more times.<br /> <br /> Building on that, they might use various fronts as a buffer. Maybe its one of the vampires considered to be autarkis; or the Children of Osiris; or a pawn in a Gehenna Cult; a scholar they're helping in another guise; perhaps even a human in the Arcanum. The PC might not even know the person helping them was part of the plan of an Inconnu. And he might be approached by a different front or pawn at each stage, not even suspecting it's one person putting out a bread trail for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T15:02:28-07:00","id":1445716,"title":"","content":"The Inconnu were the unknown watchers back in the old days and first presented in Chicago by Night (Rebekah not being the best example on how they operated) and A World of Darkness (Cret being the lone Hunedoara elder mentioned). As antagonists to the Tal'mahe'Ra in 2nd ed, a bit on their origins in Dark Ages, further expanded in Children of the Night and Lair of the Hidden in revised, and some quotes within both later editions.<br /> <br /> If you are prone to detail towards the methuselahs jyhads through the eras worldwide, using them is extremely satisfying. I liked those presented in CotN and their motives explained in LotH, but tying both was problematic, they don't seem to relate much with each other. I remember when LotH came out I was extremely hyped on the Inconnu being explained but as though the book was fine and the character interactions was interesting, it felt bland towards the scope on what the Inconnu was thought to be.<br /> <br /> White-wolf later metaplot books always fell short of their hype like The Red Sign and Gehenna, they had amazing concepts but they never achieved the epicness of what their readers expected. Through a combination of events, dedicated STs can tie the Inconnu through events like Mon\u00e7ada diablerizing Silvester de Ruiz during the beginning of the Anarch Revolt, the appearance of Count Jocalo in Madrid and the disappearance of an elder around the same time while Hauzal is monitor in the city of Madrid. Another one is the resurgence of Augustyn, Calebros' sire at the end of the clan novel tied to his sire contacting the Inconnu through Dondinni. I'm currently using them a lot though from behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T22:46:37-07:00","id":1447694,"title":"","content":"Inconnu to me are a convenient means to kick up your Chronicle's field of play from the street level into the greater arena of the Jyhad. The subtle machinations of Elders, the broad strokes of the Sect Wars, the hidden historical causes for tonight's conflicts.... in the Monitor (or their agents) you have an NPC who can simply exposit on these things without having to rely on Players' ability to put the pieces together, or to spend table time gathering clues and putting all the ducks in a row, etc. Such contrivances shouldn't be overused, but at the right place and time they can be a godsend for the Storyteller. WHY the Monitor (or their proxy) chooses to reveal themselves to the PCs and the plausibility of that reason is down to the Storyteller's ability to contrive a plausible setting and chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T19:26:24-07:00","id":1447754,"title":"","content":"What if the player characters are a Regency coterie, as described in the V5 core book, only to eventually discover that the absent elder whose estate and affairs they're managing was actually an Inconnu? One could build an entire chronicle around the implications of that discovery.<br /> <br /> I actually think that's gonna be the plot of my next campaign...I guess the elder will turn out to have been murdered, and the player characters must delve into his long past, hinted at through a plethora of artifacts in his vast haven, to find out what happened and avenge him, and set things right with the Inconnu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","user":"Natsymir","date":". 05-06-2021, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}